course: dictionary
lesson: 2593
title: Deny: say no, or refuse
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Deny is a verb, and it has three main meanings. To deny something is to say it is not true. «Sam denied breaking the vase» means Sam said he did not break it, even if he did.
explain: The second meaning is about yourself. To deny that you did something is to say you did not do it. The third meaning is about giving. To deny someone something is to refuse to give or allow it to them. «The coach denied him a place in the team» means the coach would not let him play.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. Ask: is someone saying something is false, or saying no to giving or allowing something? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Deny means to say that something is not true.
fact: To deny doing something is to say you did not do it, even when you did.
fact: To deny someone something is to refuse to give or allow it to them.
fact: In the Bible, «Peter, afraid, denied him three times», which means Peter said he did not know Jesus.
fact: Deny is a verb: deny, denies, denied, denying. «He denied it» uses the past tense.
exercise: «Sam denied breaking the vase.» What does denied mean here? | He broke it and said sorry | He paid for a new vase | He hid the broken pieces | *He said he did not break it
exercise: «The shop denied her a refund.» What does denied mean here? | Made her a cup of tea | Told her a joke | *Refused to give her the money back | Gave her a big present
exercise: Which word in «Peter, afraid, denied him three times» is the past tense of deny? | Peter | *denied | times | afraid
test: «Mia denied that she had taken the pen.» What does denied mean? | *Said it was not true | Asked for it back | Said it was true | Lost it
test: «The coach denied him a place in the team.» What does denied mean? | Asked him to lead the team | *Refused to give him a place | Sent him home early | Gave him a special badge
exam: Which meaning fits «He denied taking the last biscuit»? | He asked for another one | He ate the biscuit slowly | He said he did take it | *He said he did not take it
